!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Dirt in the tree that no lane authored: the `mempalace` and `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` submodule pointers, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`. Never commit, stash, or revert those.
* ''Landed since'' (CHANGELOG, THE HOSTED WALK, THE HOSTED WALK, MADE SOUND and THE HOSTED WALK'S AFTERMATH): the hosted walk (F1), then its cleanup (B1) — the leaf-bound retry; carriage keyed by the proven leaf; the live wallet; host and walk running inside the standing vessel over the one store door; the per-hearth hosting doc; the node's `lares walk` verbs, walking and hosting as the worn face, at one hearth; a charterless herm answering the knock (`ownPlacePosture`); a vessel under `LAR_ROOT` projecting into that root; ROOT-ON-FOUNDER pinned; the pinned docker mesh; the tree-clean witness; the staged `hosted-walk` acceptance — then its aftermath: the hosting modules naming only what stands, `mesh-scenarios` reading a hearth whose latest boot died as not stood, the road to Stable founding in canon, and the adapter note naming `LAR_ROOT` as the isolation knob.
* ''E2E'' (the whole staged set): 30 of 30 files — 215 passed.
* ''The witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`, what CI runs) ends on a verdict table, one line per witness with its own exit code — count the reds there, never in the transcript. 34 of 34 read ok, `tree-clean-witness` included (the node e2e config, `LAR_BAGS` unset, leaves the tracked tree clean). Each dist-reading witness refuses a stale build by name (exit 2) — rebuild the named package, run `node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <name>`, re-run; a comment edit in a package's `src/` stales its dist too. CI's witnesses job also runs every `tools/*.test.mjs` (53 tests).
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): every package clean across 11 projects.
* ''Unit suites'' (every suite green): `lararium-tw5` 1732; `lararium-mesh` 2470; `lararium-node` 1447; `lares-cli` 556; `lararium-keyhive` 146; `lararium-browser` 145; `lararium-web` 9; `lararium-memetic-frame` 357; `lararium-sensorium` 952 Python + 54 vitest. The tree-sitter carrier grammar reads clean.
* ''HEADS-UP — the operator's live `~/.lares` vessel'': its stored device edges were signed over the clocked layout, and any rotated seal lineage it holds carries no signed rolls. Both fail verification on this build. Do NOT stand that vessel on this build; it needs a fresh start, by hand (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/fresh-start`).
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the operator pushes; `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names the run for the pushed head, and anything committed after it waits for the next push. `held-out.yml` parses again (`00c679e97`) and runs weekly or by hand; no hosted run of it has yet read green.
* ''The docker mesh'' (by hand; `witness-all` runs none of it): `crossing-witness` 4 of 4; `node tools/mesh-pins.mjs --up` stands the mesh pinned; `herm-mesh-witness` carries `node/alpha` across three hops, verified at the last; `mesh-scenarios nexus` reads every step ok, the hearths carrying from the herm. A hearth whose log carries a `[lararium] fatal:` line reads as not stood.
* ''Known environmental reds'': `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` fail when a browser or server socket is missing.

